payload.description:
Ryan (2026-10-21): the responsive design should fill the available viewport width and make better use of screen space on very wide displays, such as a 27-inch 5K Studio Display or larger external monitors. Today the layout stops at a fixed max width (1312px in the design), which leaves wide empty margins.
Ideas to evaluate against the design:
- wide breakpoints (e.g. ≥1600, ≥2200, ≥2800px) that add columns rather than stretching text;
- the board gaining side rails (Rising, Vapor log, trending topics) beside the main list;
- item pages showing evidence, scores and related items in a side column;
- type and spacing scaling with clamp();
- reading measure capped around 68–75ch for prose, so line length stays readable.
Check at 1440, 1920, 2560 (Studio Display at default scaling), 3008 and 5120 CSS px, in light and dark; mobile and tablet must not regress. Placeholder treatment applies to any new rail that isn’t real yet.
